  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nECU-B b27: DI 10 anti-theft input - the wire is drawn on ST185-AntiTheft (broken off)\nSP-SHIELD-B (splice): drain T-splice about 6 mm (0.25 in) behind the ECU-B plug (Daniel 2026-10-12). The knock drain is the one crimped into B17 (the wire into B17 is its last few mm); every other loom-B drain (ETB motor, VSS, CAN trunk drain from ST185-CAN, rear WS spur, front WS FR spur) is soldered onto it where 6 mm of its insulation is cut away. Drains stay 20 AWG - no combined-gauge pigtail, one wire per pin.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 4260,
        "y": 1740
      },
      "width": 390
    },
    {
      "id": "n_drb102",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 4260,
        "y": 2160
      },
      "text": "BULKHEAD = ONE DRB102 CONNECTOR (Daniel 2026-10-12, shared-connector rule). bh_b_fw is the whole 102-cavity receptacle with TE's cavity numbers. A and B are only our names for its sections. Cavities marked N/C here are wired on ST185-A-cabin - see ST185-A-cabin (DRB 1-2, 9-42, 44-47, 50-53, 56-59, 61); their contacts and sealing plugs are counted there."
    }
  ],
